<title>SPAIN: Bank of Spain seen selling pesetas vs mark/dollar. [CORRECTED 13:33 GMT]</title>
<headline>Bank of Spain seen selling pesetas vs mark/dollar. [CORRECTED 13:33 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline and text to show Bank of Spain was selling and not buying pesetas against the mark.)</p>
<p>The Bank of Spain was seen selling pesetas against the mark and dollar in the currency market on Thursday to brake its rapid strengthening, Madrid dealers said.</p>
<p>The central bank declined to comment.</p>
<p>Dealers said they believed the central bank was selling pesetas around 84.83-85 against the mark.</p>
</text>
